				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# Goal\n\nAdd an ecosystem-wide query path to {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityOsvClient}}'s world — so calls like \"show me all npm risks in the last 7 days\" or \"last 14 days across npm + PyPI + crates.io\" work **without the caller enumerating packages**.\n\nThe existing {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityOsvClient}} goes through OSV's REST query API (`POST /v1/query`) which **requires a package descriptor**. That means there is no REST-shaped path to \"all npm vulns\" and there never will be — verified against the OSV REST docs, NVD v2 REST docs, and GitHub GraphQL docs on 2026-04-14.\n\nThe OSV project publishes the actual ecosystem-wide data as **bulk feeds on GCS**, and those feeds are the canonical source for ecosystem-level queries."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-14T23:11:18.877724-04:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-14T23:14:01.774665-04:00"
					}
