				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "H9bnLZ0NTZOTSPg2d6IJmw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# What the 4 candidate APIs actually support\n\nVerified against the OSV REST docs, NVD v2 REST docs, and GitHub GraphQL docs on 2026-04-14. Summary table follows inline; key takeaways:\n\n- OSV REST (`/v1/query`, `/v1/querybatch`) requires a package descriptor — no ecosystem-only path.\n- OSV bulk feed covers the full OSV corpus for every ecosystem, with a `modified_id.csv` for date filtering, and needs no auth.\n- NVD v2 has no ecosystem concept; everything is CPE-shaped.\n- GitHub GraphQL splits the capability: `securityVulnerabilities` has an `ecosystem` argument but no `publishedSince`; `securityAdvisories` has `publishedSince` but no `ecosystem`.\n\n**Implication**: the OSV bulk feed is the only path that covers full OSV + date filtering + ecosystem filtering in one place. GitHub GraphQL is useful as a secondary source (richer severity data for GHSAs) but isn't a replacement."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "elementSnippet",
