				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# OSV bulk feed — URLs and sizes (verified 2026-04-14)\n\nBase: `https://storage.googleapis.com/osv-vulnerabilities`\n\n- `/ecosystems.txt` — canonical list (41 ecosystems today: AlmaLinux, Alpine, Android, Bitnami, CRAN, Chainguard, Debian, GHC, GSD, GitHub Actions, Go, Hackage, Hex, Julia, Linux, Maven, NuGet, OSS-Fuzz, Packagist, Pub, PyPI, Red Hat, Rocky Linux, RubyGems, SUSE, SwiftURL, Ubuntu, VSCode, Wolfi, crates.io, Echo, Root, UVI, MinimOS, Mageia, npm, Alpaquita, BellSoft Hardened Containers, CleanStart, GIT, [EMPTY])\n- `/modified_id.csv` — incremental feed, sorted by modification timestamp, format `<ISO timestamp>,<ecosystem>/<ID>`. ~41 MB today.\n- `/<ECOSYSTEM>/all.zip` — full per-ecosystem dump as a zip of `<ID>.json` files.\n- `/<ECOSYSTEM>/<ID>.json` — individual vuln records (a few KB each).\n\nPer-ecosystem zip sizes follow inline. **Design implication**: for \"recent N days\" queries, prefer `modified_id.csv` + per-ID fetch (bounded by the number of recently-changed vulns, not by ecosystem size). Only fall back to `all.zip` when the caller explicitly wants a full dump. For npm specifically (192 MB), never download the full zip by default — require an explicit opt-in flag."
			},
