				},
				"string" : "## Private primitives\n- `downloadModifiedIds` — GET `modified_id.csv`, honor `If-Modified-Since` via `Last-Modified` header; cache parsed rows\n- `parseModifiedRow: aRowString` → `{ timestamp. ecosystem. id }` association\n- `fetchEcosystem:id:` → {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityVulnerability}} via a single HTTP GET on `<ECOSYSTEM>/<ID>.json`, parsed through `Gt4SecurityVulnerability fromOsvDictionary:`\n- `downloadEcosystemZip:to:` — write zip to cacheDirectory; return the file reference\n- `unzipAndParse:` — `ZipArchive readFrom:`, decode each entry, parse each JSON, return a group\n\n## Concurrency\n\nFeed fetches are I/O-bound and benefit from parallelism. Use `TKTCommonQueueWorkerPool` (or whatever GT already uses for parallel HTTP) for `recentSince:ecosystems:` to fetch the N individual JSONs concurrently with a small bounded pool (say 8). If GT doesn't expose a clean parallel-HTTP helper, start serial and measure — for \"last 7 days\" the N is typically small enough (low hundreds) that serial is acceptable."
			},
			{
