				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# Phased delivery plan\n\n## Phase 1 — Primitives + `modified_id.csv` parsing\n\nDeliverables:\n- {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityOsvFeedClient}} class with `baseUrl`, `cacheDirectory`, `history` ivars and default initializer\n- `downloadModifiedIds` — ZnClient GET with Last-Modified caching to disk\n- `parseModifiedIds:` — returns an `OrderedCollection` of `{ timestamp. ecosystem. id }` associations\n- `fetchEcosystem:id:` — single-vuln GET, parse through `Gt4SecurityVulnerability fromOsvDictionary:`\n- `<gtExample>` methods covering: CSV parse with synthetic input (offline), Last-Modified round-trip (offline), and a live single-vuln lookup (`<noTest>`)\n- GT Summary view showing cache state, row count, last fetch time\n\n**Definition of done**: `Gt4SecurityOsvFeedClient new fetchEcosystem: 'npm' id: 'GHSA-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx'` returns a parsed vuln.\n\n## Phase 2 — `recentSince:ecosystems:` aggregator\n\nDeliverables:\n- `recentSince:ecosystems:` — parses cached `modified_id.csv`, filters by `timestamp > cutoff` and `ecosystem in allowlist`, fans out to `fetchEcosystem:id:`, wraps in a {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityVulnerabilityGroup}}\n- `recentSince:` — convenience that passes the full ecosystems list\n- Offline `<gtExample>` using a stub feed client that returns canned rows + canned JSONs\n- Live `<gtExample>` `<noTest>` for last 7 days npm\n- Progress reporting: use a `GtJob` wrapper so long fetches show a progress bar in the inspector\n\n**Definition of done**: `Gt4SecurityOsvFeedClient new recentSince: Date today - 7 days ecosystems: #('npm' 'PyPI')` returns a non-empty group in under a minute; result group's existing `gtByEcosystemFor:` shows real ecosystem breakdown (npm: N, PyPI: M).\n\n## Phase 3 — Full-dump path `ecosystemFull:`\n\nDeliverables:\n- `downloadEcosystemZip:` — writes `<eco>/all.zip` to cache, keyed by ETag\n- `ecosystemFull:` — unzips via `ZipArchive readFrom:`, parses each entry, returns a group\n- `ecosystemFull:acceptLargeDownload:` — npm-size guard; requires explicit opt-in\n- `<gtExample>` live on crates.io (2.5 MB, quick) `<noTest>`\n- Size guard threshold configurable; default 50 MB\n\n**Definition of done**: full crates.io dump parses into a group of ~700 vulns with correct ecosystems.\n\n## Phase 4 — `Gt4SecurityQuery` integration + demo\n\nDeliverables:\n- `Gt4SecurityQuery >> feedRecentSince:ecosystems:`\n- `Gt4SecurityQuery >> feedClient:` / `feedClient`\n- Extend {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityQueryResult}} with `feedCount` + provenance view updates\n- Live demo example `Gt4SecurityQueryExamples >> feedScanWeek` — \"last 7 days across npm + PyPI + crates.io\"\n- A Playground cell on the Playground page demonstrating the feed path\n- Update the Demo page's cross-source overview to mention feed source\n\n**Definition of done**: `Gt4SecurityQueryExamples new feedScanWeek` returns a `Gt4SecurityQueryResult` where `feedCount + nvdCount + osvCount = total`.\n\n## Phase 5 (optional) — GitHub GraphQL client\n\nOnly if Phase 1-4 prove insufficient for some use case (e.g. richer severity/patch metadata). Lower priority — the OSV feed already covers everything GHSA publishes to OSV. Skip unless there's a concrete gap."
			},
