					"uidString" : "AtfsedlTQmOJcOL2n5XAwg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# Edge cases and gotchas to watch for\n\n- **`modified_id.csv` grows unbounded** — today ~41 MB, ever-growing. Cache it to disk; only re-GET when `Last-Modified` changes (or on explicit refresh). Do NOT re-download per call.\n- **Timestamps are modification, not publication** — a recent row means the record was *touched* (possibly a metadata fix). If the caller wants strictly \"newly disclosed\", filter the resulting group by `v published > cutoff` after fetching, not by CSV timestamp alone.\n- **[EMPTY] row in `ecosystems.txt`** — literally one of the entries. Filter it out in the ecosystems list.\n- **CPE-shaped vulns**: the OSV feed does NOT contain CPE-only entries — those are NVD's domain. Ecosystem feeds are OSV-native, so the `Gt4SecurityVulnerability >> hasCpeAffected` predicate will be `false` for all feed results. That's expected.\n- **Malicious package records** ride inline in npm/PyPI/etc. feeds — they'll appear naturally in results; the existing `malicious` / `benign` filters on {{gtClass:Gt4SecurityVulnerabilityGroup}} already handle them.\n- **`ZipArchive readFrom:`** expects a `ReadStream` on bytes — use a binary read stream on the downloaded zip file, not a text stream.\n- **HTTP failure modes**: `modified_id.csv` or individual JSONs may 404 if the ID was withdrawn. Log + skip, don't crash the whole sweep.\n- **Rate limiting**: GCS has no documented per-IP rate limit for public buckets, but being polite — cap concurrent fetches to 8 and back off on 429/5xx."
			},
			{
