				"string" : "# Mobile-ecosystem deliverable (live data)\n\n`Gt4SecurityQueryExamples new mobileFeedLast90Days` run on 2026-04-15. 9,127 per-ID HTTP fetches across the mobile-relevant OSV ecosystems, 249 s end-to-end, 0 errors, 200 cross-ecosystem duplicates deduped, 3,740 final vulnerabilities (published within the last 90 days) across 2,582 unique packages.\n\nPer-ecosystem breakdown follows as an inline table.\n\nTop-line observations:\n- **npm dominates** (3,181 / 85% of the mobile attack surface) — the React Native / Expo / Capacitor / Cordova / Ionic / NativeScript cluster. Of those, **60% are MAL-* malicious-package reports** (single-use attacker packages, flat distribution of 1 report per package).\n- **Android platform ids modify often, publish rarely** — 3,261 rows were modified in the window but only 121 are freshly published. Most modifications are metadata updates to older CVEs (new Pixel patch levels, added vendor backports).\n- **Maven = enterprise-backend territory**: Keycloak (27), Tomcat (13+12+12), ActiveMQ (5). Relevant to apps with embedded Java or Java backends.\n- **NuGet `Magick.NET` wave**: one library's build variants took 85-87 advisories each in a concentrated window — interesting anomaly worth a second look.\n- **Swift/Flutter are effectively quiet** (6 SwiftURL + 1 Pub). Either real scarcity or under-reporting into OSV.\n\nReproducible via: `Gt4SecurityQueryExamples new mobileFeedLast90Days`. First run downloads `modified_id.csv` (~40 MB) to the local cache at `FileLocator temp / gt4security-osv-feed /`; subsequent runs reuse the cache, so repeat runs of the example complete in 3-5 minutes."
			},
